course: dictionary
lesson: 8828
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. «Shield» can name a thing or describe an action. The words around it give you the clue. In «Their best fighters were knights... who painted coats of arms on their shields», the shields are things that soldiers and knights carry, so shield is a noun, a naming word.
explain: Now read «The Earth's magnetic field shields us from most of the solar wind.» Here shields is something the field does, so shield is a verb. Ask: is someone or something doing an action? Then swap in a meaning: "The Earth's magnetic field protects us from most of the solar wind." It still makes sense, so shield means protect here.
explain: The same check works for «shield your eyes from the Sun». Swap in protect: "protect your eyes from the Sun" makes sense, so this shield is a verb telling you what to do. One word can change its shape too: a shield, to shield, shielded, shielding. Look at the small words around it to find out which job it is doing.
fact: Shield can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: As a noun, a shield is a large flat piece of metal, wood or other material that protects a soldier or knight in battle.
fact: As a noun, a shield can also be anything that protects you, such as a heat shield or a sun shield.
fact: As a verb, to shield someone or something means to protect it from harm or danger.
fact: A shield can also be a badge or a trophy shaped like a shield.
exercise: «Their best fighters were knights, who carried shields in battle.» In this sentence, what is a shield? | A flag that shows the way home | A loud war cry | *A large flat piece of metal or wood held for protection | A kind of horse ridden into battle
exercise: «The Earth's magnetic field shields us from most of the solar wind.» Which word means the same as shields here? | paints | *protects | fights | heats
exercise: «A heat shield protects a spacecraft.» Which word tells you what a heat shield does? | heat | shield | spacecraft | *protects
test: Read «Shield your eyes from the Sun.» Is shield a noun or a verb here? | Neither, it is a name | Adjective, because it describes the eyes | Noun, because it names a thing | *Verb, because it tells you to do something
test: «A gum shield should be rinsed in cold water and kept in its case.» What is a gum shield? | A type of rash | A sugary drink that feeds germs | A towel for the showers | *A piece of gear that protects your teeth and gums when you play sport
exam: Which sentence uses shield as a verb? | *Please shield your eyes from the bright Sun | A heat shield keeps the spacecraft safe | The windscreen was cracked | The knight raised his shield high
